    faqs: [{ question: "What is the first step in triage voicemail so outsourced call center follow-up starts with the right facts?", answer: "Define the fields to capture, the urgent triggers, the duplicate rule, the callback owner, and the handling of messages that lack enough identity or purpose to proceed. Keep the audio or source reference linked where permitted." }, { question: "What boundary matters for triage voicemail so outsourced call center follow-up starts with the right facts?", answer: "The triage role can transcribe relevant facts, classify the request, and use approved follow-up wording. It should not guess the account, disclose information to an unverified caller, or treat a vague message as permission for broad action." }, { question: "How should a manager review triage voicemail so outsourced call center follow-up starts with the right facts?", answer: "Review transcription accuracy, incomplete-message rate, urgent recognition, duplicate creation, callback age, and wrong-owner assignments. Inspect both false urgency and missed urgency because either distorts the queue." }],
